# RoadRunner worker binary.
# `bin/rr` is a downloaded release asset (~62 MB), not source. It was sitting
# untracked in the working tree with no ignore rule, so an unguarded
# `git add -A` would have committed a 62 MB binary into the repository.
/bin/rr

# Ad-hoc per-zone Infection configs.
# The canonical config is /infection.json5. The committed
# infection-chunk-*.json5 and infection-fullrun.json5 files are historical
# campaign records (mapped in docs/QUALITY.md). Generated per-zone configs
# (e.g. `infection-zone-<name>.json5`, written by the mutation-campaign
# tooling at the repository root because Infection resolves relative source
# paths against the CONFIG FILE's directory) must never be committed.
/infection-zone-*.json5
